Package: disperseR
Title: Classification of Animal Movements
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Cesar", "Herraiz", email = "c.herraizfer@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4770-2013"))
Description: Tools to segment and classify animal movement trajectories,
    with a focus on long-range movements. Tracks can be regularised with
    continuous-time movement models from 'ctmm' and classified into
    behavioural states with hidden Markov models from 'momentuHMM'.
    Area-restricted phases (ARP) are then identified with density-based
    spatial clustering ('dbscan'), linked through time, and the movements
    between them are classified according to the spatial network of
    previously visited areas (unanchored movement, loops, network expansion
    and internal transit).
